# Ocentra Parent Rule Index

Read this file before coding in this repo. It is a router, not the whole rulebook.

## Core Rule

Do not add product behavior until the relevant scaffold boundary exists, is typed, and is validated.

## Rust-First Architecture Rule

Current parent architecture is Rust-first. Product flow is TSX UI through
HostBridge into the Rust parent app facade, Rust event bus/domain, Rust read
models, then back through HostBridge to TSX UI. Dev web may use a local dev
transport for Codex/HMR only. Vite/web is not a product target and must not be
described as product truth.

Rust owns contracts, schemas, route snapshots, action handling, read models,
projections, business logic, policy/activity/tracking/network/browser/
enforcement/logging shapes, mobile bridge shapes, and product proof logs.
TypeScript is presentation only or generated/thin edge code: TSX, CSS, assets,
generated bridge DTO/types, thin host/dev adapters, and minimal local visual
state. TypeScript must not be the source of product contracts or business
logic.

When an older plan says `schema-domain`, `agent-protocol-domain`, a feature TS
domain package, WebSocket, or Vite portal owns product truth, treat that wording
as migration/debt unless a current Rust-first route explicitly says otherwise.
Do not restate those older ownership claims in new docs or rules.

## Universal Logging and Proof-Chain Rule

This rule is repo-wide, not Cloudflare-only.

Before editing runtime behavior, service code, domain behavior, app command paths, proof helpers, tests, scripts, or Rust crates involved in a command/event/request/read-model chain, read:

- `.ocentra-ai/rules/ocentra-parent-logging-redaction.mdc`
- `docs/repo-audits/event-driven-proof-architecture/LOGGER_USAGE_PATTERN_STANDARD.md`
- `docs/repo-audits/event-driven-proof-architecture/LOGGED_PROOF_CHAIN_STANDARD.md`

New or edited core chain files must be logger-ready unless they are pure schema, constants, brands, generated data, or static docs. Runtime logs stay gated and redacted. Tests, proof scripts, and dev command routes must emit correlated proof milestones when they prove a chain.

## Product Feature Doc Route

For product-facing work, route by feature before routing by code layer:

1. Read `docs/feature-list.md`.
2. Read the one matching `docs/features/*.md` file.
3. Read only the expectation docs linked by that feature doc that match the task.
4. Read the touched module README before editing that module.
5. Update the feature doc and `docs/product-capability-checklist.md` if status, proof, or gap changes.

Do not bulk-load all roadmap, expectation, feature, or checkpoint docs. Open
historical checkpoint files only when the current feature doc, checklist,
roadmap, or hub assignment names them as proof.

